// The option chain of one underlying, for the `chain` topic (WP-1.2; MKT-04 to MKT-06, PRC-13,
// REF-03, SUB-05). Decided 2026-11-28 (requirements, section 3, "The chain package"). The topic,
// its windows and the message of the topic are in channel.proto.
//
// A subscription names the underlying and its windows: an expiration and a range of strikes
// each. The backend subscribes those contracts only, never a whole chain. The snapshot carries
// every open expiration of the underlying and the rows of the windows; later messages carry what
// changed. A whole expiration, every strike, comes over REST as Arrow (API-06), with the columns
// of ChainRows.
//
// The rules of market.proto hold for numbers, instants and columns. Greeks are spot Greeks in
// trader units with a multiplier and a quantity of 1, that is per share: delta as a fraction,
// gamma per dollar of the underlying, theta in dollars a calendar day, vega in dollars a
// volatility point (requirements 4.6). A date is ISO text, `2026-12-18`.

